From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matt chow <zhoujinliang@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:34:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] seahelm: report OSC 7501 program status to the embedder

Port the OSC 7501 (Program Status Protocol, rev 0.4) parser from upstream
9cd19b40d (#14560, #14630) onto 12967b68f, then wire it through the app
path, which upstream still drops:

- termio answers the support query (OSC 7501 ; ?) and forwards reports
  to the surface; RIS reports a clear of every record
- Surface decodes each report and performs a new apprt action,
  GHOSTTY_ACTION_PROGRAM_STATUS (appended, so existing ordinals hold)
- the strings ride behind a pointer so ghostty_action_u stays 24 bytes

The libghostty-vt C API for program status is not ported; GhosttyKit does
not use it. The query is answered unconditionally because this build only
serves an embedder that consumes the reports.
